{
  "_comment": "Whitelist of Athena tables published as static JSON every 4h by scripts/fetch_data.R. To add a new table: append an object below and set enabled=true. To deprecate: set enabled=false (the file is left untouched on disk). Columns are inlined per-table; rows from Athena are projected to that subset before write. Special per-table filtering (e.g., date cutoffs) is keyed by the 'filter' field and implemented in fetch_data.R.",
  "_discover": {
    "_comment": "Used by scripts/discover_tables.R (triggered manually via .github/workflows/discover-tables.yml). Tables matching match_regex on Athena that are not already in 'tables' below get appended as disabled stubs.",
    "match_regex": "^(vitrine_datamart|agora_datamart)-"
  },
  "_calibration": {
    "_comment": "NOT a table projection — computed by build_salience_calibration() in fetch_data.R (suivi aws-refiners#212). Publishes rolling-window percentiles (p5/p20/p50/p80/p95) of score_qc, score_roc and interval_convergence_score to public/data/salience_calibration.json. The frontend (lib/data/headlineEvents.ts) derives SAL_QC_THRESHOLDS and CAL_CONV from it, falling back to hardcoded values if the file is absent or a metric is missing.",
    "out": "public/data/salience_calibration.json",
    "window_days": 365
  },
  "tables": [
